---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import fish from "../../data/fish.json";

const topFarm = [...fish]
  .filter((f) => Number(f.meat_per_day) > 0)
  .sort((a, b) => Number(b.meat_per_day || 0) - Number(a.meat_per_day || 0))
  .slice(0, 10);

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  headline: "How to Unlock the Fish Farm in Dave the Diver",
  description: "Fish Farm unlock steps, Otto's tank upgrades and the best farm strategy.",
  datePublished: "2026-08-20",
  dateModified: "2026-08-20",
  author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "DiverDB" },
};
---

<Base
  title="How to Unlock the Fish Farm - Dave the Diver - DiverDB"
  description="How to unlock the Fish Farm in Dave the Diver, complete A Noisy Customer and use Otto's tanks."
  schema={articleSchema}
>
  <h1>How to Unlock the Fish Farm</h1>
  <p class="muted">
    The Fish Farm opens after the Chapter 2 sub mission A Noisy Customer.
  </p>

  <h2>Unlock steps</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Reach Chapter 2 and wait for Bancho's call about a noisy customer.</li>
    <li>Dive at night to catch a moray eel.</li>
    <li>Research and serve Moray Eel Curry.</li>
    <li>Talk to Otto after the restaurant closes.</li>
    <li>Meet Otto at the empty lot behind Bancho Sushi.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Starting this mission also unlocks <strong>Night Diving</strong>, which is required for nocturnal
    fish and several achievements.
  </p>

  <h2>What the farm does</h2>
  <p>
    The farm has sections for each Blue Hole biome. Otto sells tank upgrades and new area unlocks.
    Two fish of the same species can breed, and caught eggs or roe can be sent to the farm when tank
    space is available.
  </p>

  <h2>Top farm stock after unlock</h2>
  <div style="overflow-x:auto">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Fish</th>
          <th>Meat / day</th>
          <th>Breed cap</th>
          <th>Breed rate</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {topFarm.map((f) => (
          <tr>
            <td><strong>{f.title}</strong></td>
            <td>{f.meat_per_day}</td>
            <td>{f.breed_cap || "—"}</td>
            <td>{f.breed_rate || "—"}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    Filter and rank candidates with the <a href="/tools/fish-farm/">Fish Farm Planner</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
